<%- include('../partials/head', {
  title: 'Accessibility',
  canonicalPath: '/accessibility',
  description: 'How RYDJA approaches website accessibility, what we have done so far, and how to tell us when something does not work for you.'
}) %>

<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="section shell narrow legal">
  <div class="eyebrow">ACCESSIBILITY</div>
  <h1>Accessibility</h1>
  <p class="lede smaller">
    We want this site to be usable by as many people as possible, including people who use a keyboard, a screen
    reader, magnification, or a browser set to reduce motion.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we are</h2>
  <p>
    We work to make the site accessible and we keep improving it. We have not had the site independently audited or
    certified, so <strong>we do not claim to be ADA compliant or WCAG conformant</strong> &mdash; those are claims that
    should be earned by assessment, not asserted on a web page. What we can tell you is what we have actually done.
  </p>

  <h2>What we have done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every form field has a visible label attached to it, not just placeholder text</li>
    <li>The whole site can be operated by keyboard, and focused elements show a visible focus ring</li>
    <li>A skip link lets keyboard and screen reader users jump straight past the navigation to the page content</li>
    <li>Pages have one main heading and a sensible heading order</li>
    <li>Images carry alternative text; decorative artwork is marked so assistive software skips it</li>
    <li>Form errors are described in words next to the form, and are announced rather than shown only by colour</li>
    <li>Status is never communicated by colour alone &mdash; labels carry the meaning too</li>
    <li>Native date, time and select controls are used, so your own device's accessibility features work normally</li>
    <li>Movement on the site is subtle and switches off entirely if your system is set to reduce motion</li>
    <li>Text is sized in a way that respects your browser's zoom and font settings</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known limitations</h2>
  <p>
    The hero area uses a dark background with a light illustration behind the headline. We have set the contrast to
    stay readable, but if any text on this site is hard for you to read, we want to know.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell us when something does not work</h2>
  <p>
    If any part of this site is difficult or impossible for you to use, contact us and we will help you directly and
    fix the problem where we can. You should never have to fight the website to get a quote &mdash; we will take your
    job over the phone.
  </p>
  <p>
    <% if (businessPhone) { %>Call or text <a class="text-link" href="tel:<%= telHref(businessPhone) %>"><%= businessPhone %></a><% } %><% if (businessEmail) { %><% if (businessPhone) { %>, or email<% } else { %>Email<% } %> <a class="text-link" href="mailto:<%= businessEmail %>"><%= businessEmail %></a><% } %>.
    Please tell us the page and what went wrong, and we will come back to you.
  </p>

  <p class="legal-foot">Last updated: October 2026</p>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
